  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-forensic art direction, crisp headline contrast, disciplined cyan/red palette, and polished cards. Desktop composition is compelling, but tablet becomes vertically sparse and disconnected; mobile loses the visual connector narrative and feels like a long stack. The global header visibly clips navigation at tablet/mobile widths, with truncated items and no clear overflow cue. Tiny, low-contrast mono labels also weaken readability, and contrast verification remains incomplete across 14–26 header nodes.",
    "fix": "Redesign the responsive header with an explicit menu or visible horizontal-scroll affordance; preserve simplified connector lines on mobile; tighten tablet spacing; and increase the size/contrast of micro-labels after testing them against the actual gradient background.",
